WEBVTT

00:01:42.930 --> 00:01:45.040
Well done, everyone.

00:01:47.670 --> 00:01:51.630
The fate of Kishuu rests in 
the hands of you craftsmen.

00:01:54.170 --> 00:01:55.260
Continue.

00:01:56.190 --> 00:01:57.130
Yes, sir.

00:02:05.940 --> 00:02:08.520
No snack, Juuzou.

00:02:09.190 --> 00:02:10.760
I know.

00:02:14.990 --> 00:02:16.230
What's wrong, Saizou?

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:17.900
You look dismayed.

00:02:18.910 --> 00:02:23.200
The Rokurou pair went to find
 the intruders, and haven't returned.

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:25.070
It is not a concern.

00:02:25.070 --> 00:02:30.750
Indeed, the Rokurou pair would 
never lose to mere humans.

00:02:31.170 --> 00:02:34.170
<b>Wanted</b>

00:02:31.720 --> 00:02:33.390
I hope not...

00:02:37.710 --> 00:02:40.800
We're almost there, miss.

00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:41.470
Yes.

00:02:44.460 --> 00:02:45.660
I can see it!

00:02:45.660 --> 00:02:47.800
That must be the temple.

00:02:53.060 --> 00:02:55.110
Miss, stay here.

00:02:57.150 --> 00:02:58.780
You, there...

00:02:58.780 --> 00:03:01.570
What are you doing?

00:03:04.010 --> 00:03:06.580
<b>Time's Up! 
The Insect Magistrate's Office Arrives!</b>

00:03:06.580 --> 00:03:09.460
You, there! What are you doing?

00:03:12.130 --> 00:03:14.540
I'm with the Insect Magistrate's!

00:03:14.950 --> 00:03:16.750
I know that, you idiot, Tsukishima!

00:03:18.030 --> 00:03:19.910
Hibachi-dono?

00:03:19.910 --> 00:03:22.670
What are you doing here?

00:03:22.670 --> 00:03:25.430
And why did you just attack me?

00:03:26.170 --> 00:03:27.260
Jeez...

00:03:27.680 --> 00:03:30.110
Do you realize how long 
I've been looking for you?

00:03:30.520 --> 00:03:31.770
Stupid Tsukishima.

00:03:32.200 --> 00:03:34.610
Hibachi-dono...

00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:37.400
That's impossible!

00:03:38.690 --> 00:03:39.290
Tsukishima?

00:03:39.290 --> 00:03:41.490
Hibachi-dono is in Edo!

00:03:41.490 --> 00:03:44.870
Reveal yourself, monster!

00:03:54.070 --> 00:03:55.630
You stupid Tsukishima!

00:03:56.570 --> 00:03:58.850
That explosion...

00:03:58.850 --> 00:04:00.460
It's the real Hibachi-dono!

00:04:00.460 --> 00:04:02.380
Of course it is!

00:04:02.380 --> 00:04:05.640
What was that explosion?

00:04:05.640 --> 00:04:06.970
Hibachi-neesama?

00:04:08.740 --> 00:04:09.470
Irori?

00:04:11.770 --> 00:04:14.880
Hibachi-neesama...

00:04:16.150 --> 00:04:19.650
You came, Hibachi-neesama!

00:04:20.250 --> 00:04:23.440
Irori, I'm glad you're doing well.

00:04:23.440 --> 00:04:25.280
Neesama...

00:04:30.900 --> 00:04:34.630
It's been so long since
 I've smelled your scent...

00:04:34.630 --> 00:04:37.790
You really smells like camellia blossoms!

00:04:37.790 --> 00:04:39.880
It's so wonderful!

00:04:40.160 --> 00:04:43.420
Hibachi-dono, what are you doing here?

00:04:43.880 --> 00:04:46.970
I was told to meet up with 
you as soon as possible!

00:04:48.130 --> 00:04:49.090
Tsukishima-san!

00:04:49.090 --> 00:04:55.130
And then you went missing, 
and I couldn't find you!

00:04:55.780 --> 00:05:00.070
Then I thought perhaps this 
area's lord, Yamagatake,

00:05:00.070 --> 00:05:02.600
might know something.

00:05:02.960 --> 00:05:04.930
So I followed him.

00:05:06.880 --> 00:05:09.410
You also know Yamagatake, Hibachi-dono?

00:05:09.660 --> 00:05:11.000
Of course I do!

00:05:11.000 --> 00:05:13.420
My grandfather served his family!

00:05:14.440 --> 00:05:15.630
Wait a second.

00:05:15.630 --> 00:05:17.870
What do you mean by "also"?

00:05:18.470 --> 00:05:21.380
I shall explain that.

00:05:23.110 --> 00:05:26.380
You are the Insect Magistrate...

00:05:27.600 --> 00:05:29.890
The Magistrate's servant.

00:05:30.930 --> 00:05:32.840
M-Miss...

00:05:32.840 --> 00:05:34.890
Then you know Hibachi-dono?

00:05:34.890 --> 00:05:35.790
Yes.

00:05:36.320 --> 00:05:37.280
I've met her once.

00:05:37.280 --> 00:05:38.750
What are you talking about?

00:05:38.750 --> 00:05:41.130
She's the real Insect Magistrate...

00:05:41.130 --> 00:05:43.070
Magistrate's servant.

00:05:44.060 --> 00:05:45.560
Magistrate...

00:05:45.560 --> 00:05:47.790
Magistrate's servant.

00:05:47.790 --> 00:05:49.910
No, I mean...

00:05:50.350 --> 00:05:52.340
Magistrate's servant!

00:05:54.530 --> 00:05:56.180
Fine, then...

00:05:56.180 --> 00:05:57.540
Servant.

00:05:58.900 --> 00:06:01.360
Anyway, what's going on?

00:06:02.080 --> 00:06:03.380
You see,

00:06:04.310 --> 00:06:07.120
to infiltrate Wakayama Castle,

00:06:07.120 --> 00:06:10.060
we contacted the lord of this region,

00:06:10.060 --> 00:06:12.890
with the assistance
of some villagers we saved.

00:06:20.150 --> 00:06:22.630
You are Oooka Tadasuke-dono?

00:06:22.630 --> 00:06:26.420
Even here, in Kishuu, your fame is well-known.

00:06:26.420 --> 00:06:27.960
I am honored,

00:06:28.340 --> 00:06:30.070
Yamagatake Masashikata.

00:06:31.270 --> 00:06:33.110
And what is your answer?

00:06:33.530 --> 00:06:36.050
Your request was that, as you are fugitives,

00:06:36.050 --> 00:06:41.250
you wish to be led secretly 
to Wakayama Castle, yes?

00:06:41.590 --> 00:06:45.750
Will you risk your life to work with us?

00:06:50.950 --> 00:06:53.380
Many innocents have died

00:06:53.380 --> 00:06:57.080
at the hands of those you call the Insect-men.

00:06:57.980 --> 00:07:01.770
Will you swear that the people of Kishuu

00:07:02.280 --> 00:07:04.020
will no longer have to suffer?

00:07:04.380 --> 00:07:05.380
I swear.

00:07:05.380 --> 00:07:10.280
The Shogunate will put an end 
to the Insect-men's evil.

00:07:14.330 --> 00:07:15.700
Bizen, was it?

00:07:16.420 --> 00:07:18.690
You've done well to bring them here.

00:07:19.210 --> 00:07:20.160
I thank you.

00:07:26.900 --> 00:07:29.190
We have two days until the deadline

00:07:29.190 --> 00:07:34.050
the Insect-men gave the people 
of Kishuu people to capture us expires.

00:07:35.670 --> 00:07:38.020
I shall share my plan with you.

00:07:38.550 --> 00:07:40.300
It is a race against time.

00:07:40.300 --> 00:07:44.480
I'd like you to complete these tasks 
as soon as possible.

00:07:45.060 --> 00:07:48.110
<b>Wanted</b>

00:07:52.240 --> 00:07:55.300
In two days, time runs out.

00:07:55.300 --> 00:08:00.830
Your failure to capture the fugitives 
is due to your laziness.

00:08:00.830 --> 00:08:02.930
Prepare yourselves.

00:08:02.930 --> 00:08:07.250
You will find these people and 
bring them to Yukimura-sama,

00:08:07.250 --> 00:08:11.680
or your blood will stain the soil of Kishuu.

00:08:12.860 --> 00:08:15.120
There is little time left.

00:08:16.690 --> 00:08:18.510
There are two days remaining.

00:08:18.730 --> 00:08:21.120
No matter what, we must finish the ship,

00:08:21.120 --> 00:08:24.770
and get those insects out of Kishuu!

00:08:24.770 --> 00:08:25.970
Yeah!

00:08:30.290 --> 00:08:33.950
<i>Please make it in time, citizens of Kishuu!</i>

00:08:36.340 --> 00:08:38.120
It's been a while, kid.

00:08:38.120 --> 00:08:39.490
How've you been?

00:08:39.490 --> 00:08:40.770
We finally found you.

00:08:41.570 --> 00:08:42.700
Koikawa-dono!

00:08:42.700 --> 00:08:43.790
Tenma-dono!

00:08:44.940 --> 00:08:46.030
Mugai-dono!

00:08:46.030 --> 00:08:47.570
It's been so long!

00:08:47.570 --> 00:08:51.670
With you here, those Insect-men 
won't stand a chance.

00:08:52.660 --> 00:08:54.930
Potato-boy, I must speak with you.

00:09:02.670 --> 00:09:04.690
Onee-sama...

00:09:07.850 --> 00:09:10.150
You should get to sleep.

00:09:10.150 --> 00:09:12.290
We'll be busy tomorrow.

00:09:13.100 --> 00:09:14.040
Yeah.

00:09:17.080 --> 00:09:18.250
What's wrong?

00:09:20.600 --> 00:09:21.950
Hibachi, was it?

00:09:21.950 --> 00:09:24.920
What do you think of Tsukishima?

00:09:30.960 --> 00:09:33.410
You seem to think well of him.

00:09:33.410 --> 00:09:37.130
He's just a little bug compared to Mugai-san.

00:09:38.220 --> 00:09:39.970
But well...

00:09:40.350 --> 00:09:44.060
I guess he's a little better than he was.

00:09:46.070 --> 00:09:47.310
I see...

00:09:47.570 --> 00:09:50.900
Then from now on, I shall leave him to you.

00:09:53.280 --> 00:09:54.260
Where are you going?

00:09:54.810 --> 00:09:55.900
The bathroom.

00:10:01.430 --> 00:10:03.450
The Magistrate?

00:10:07.830 --> 00:10:12.850
Do you know the Magistrate's goal 
for this journey, potato-boy?

00:10:13.950 --> 00:10:17.720
The Magistrate's goal?

00:10:19.470 --> 00:10:20.690
What?

00:10:20.690 --> 00:10:22.970
Do you know it, Mugai-dono?

00:10:25.220 --> 00:10:27.440
What? What?

00:10:27.440 --> 00:10:30.870
Mugai-dono, did you just say 
"the Insect Magistrate"?

00:10:30.870 --> 00:10:36.610
Which means we're here on the 
Magistrate's orders, right?

00:10:39.390 --> 00:10:40.360
Indeed.

00:10:41.100 --> 00:10:42.370
Potato-boy,

00:10:43.100 --> 00:10:44.330
don't screw it up.

00:10:49.170 --> 00:10:53.560
Mugai-dono was thinking of me...

00:10:55.550 --> 00:10:57.560
Mugai-dono, just wait.

00:10:57.560 --> 00:10:59.840
I'll do my best!

00:11:01.530 --> 00:11:03.890
There you are, Tsukishima.

00:11:04.370 --> 00:11:06.270
Oh, miss servant!

00:11:07.390 --> 00:11:09.130
I couldn't sleep.

00:11:09.130 --> 00:11:11.980
Want to go somewhere with a better view?

00:11:15.710 --> 00:11:18.780
And so Koikawa-dono, you see,

00:11:18.780 --> 00:11:21.860
looks scary, like this,

00:11:21.860 --> 00:11:23.490
but he's an amazing swordsman!

00:11:23.490 --> 00:11:25.010
I see.

00:11:25.010 --> 00:11:28.990
And Tenma-dono is a noble,
 cute little boy!

00:11:28.990 --> 00:11:31.400
And he's mysterious and amazing!

00:11:31.400 --> 00:11:32.790
I see.

00:11:33.270 --> 00:11:35.170
Insects...

00:11:35.540 --> 00:11:37.150
You know Mugai-dono...

00:11:37.150 --> 00:11:40.170
He's cool, great, and so awesome!

00:11:40.650 --> 00:11:42.470
Yes, I see.

00:11:43.450 --> 00:11:45.410
Am I boring you?

00:11:45.410 --> 00:11:48.680
I'm just going on about the City Patrol...

00:11:48.680 --> 00:11:51.860
I know a great story about 
sword fighting I could tell you!

00:11:51.860 --> 00:11:54.310
No, please continue.

00:11:54.870 --> 00:11:58.900
Your stories are so warm and pleasant.

00:12:01.150 --> 00:12:03.530
Anyway, everyone's so amazing!

00:12:03.530 --> 00:12:05.670
I'm still so inexperienced.

00:12:05.670 --> 00:12:07.590
I need to practice more!

00:12:09.670 --> 00:12:10.950
Is that...

00:12:23.290 --> 00:12:28.570
I'm pretty careless, so I make sure 
to never let it leave my side.

00:12:28.570 --> 00:12:30.510
It's not that important.

00:12:31.020 --> 00:12:33.980
I told you that it's a cheap thing.

00:12:34.350 --> 00:12:38.000
No, it's important to me!

00:12:39.350 --> 00:12:44.740
I feel like this bell connects my karma to yours.

00:12:47.750 --> 00:12:52.000
Anyway, I was so amazed at Hachijo Island!

00:12:52.340 --> 00:12:55.750
I never thought I'd see you again...

00:13:01.140 --> 00:13:02.260
Indeed.

00:13:02.950 --> 00:13:05.320
You're so very warm.

00:13:06.100 --> 00:13:08.190
<i>Miss?</i>

00:13:10.210 --> 00:13:13.260
Are you cold?

00:13:13.260 --> 00:13:14.370
Oh, no!

00:13:14.370 --> 00:13:16.330
Let's return to the inn.

00:13:18.860 --> 00:13:20.400
There's no need.

00:13:22.940 --> 00:13:26.370
Instead, allow me stay 
like this for a moment...

00:13:27.080 --> 00:13:28.470
Okay!

00:13:28.470 --> 00:13:30.280
Hold on tight!

00:13:34.850 --> 00:13:37.560
<i>Yes... Just for now.</i>

00:13:38.170 --> 00:13:40.040
<i>So that once this journey ends,</i>

00:13:40.380 --> 00:13:43.770
<i>I will not forget your warmth.</i>

00:13:47.250 --> 00:13:49.560
Y-You can't do that!

00:13:49.560 --> 00:13:53.060
Holding a girl's hand this late...

00:13:55.350 --> 00:13:57.020
What are you doing, Tenma?

00:13:59.280 --> 00:14:01.310
There he is.

00:14:01.700 --> 00:14:05.450
The servant is with Tsukishima!

00:14:05.450 --> 00:14:07.510
Oh, hey, everyone!

00:14:07.510 --> 00:14:09.320
Let's go, miss!

00:14:11.920 --> 00:14:14.480
You already know Hibachi-dono, right?

00:14:14.480 --> 00:14:17.670
I'll introduce you to 
Koikawa-dono and Tenma-dono!

00:14:21.650 --> 00:14:24.360
Yes, please do.

00:14:25.810 --> 00:14:27.280
Hey, kid...

00:14:27.280 --> 00:14:30.320
You're looking stronger lately.

00:14:30.320 --> 00:14:31.580
Really?

00:14:31.580 --> 00:14:32.620
I don't know.

00:14:32.620 --> 00:14:34.230
But you and Tenma-dono...

00:14:34.230 --> 00:14:37.770
Um, well... Sorry.

00:14:38.970 --> 00:14:43.010
It feels like we interrupted 
you and Tsukishima.

00:14:43.660 --> 00:14:45.450
No, it's fine.

00:14:48.640 --> 00:14:52.660
In its own way, this is fun.

00:14:55.200 --> 00:14:58.470
<i>Then from now on, I shall leave him to you.</i>

00:14:59.320 --> 00:15:02.550
<i>What did she mean by that?</i>

00:15:23.960 --> 00:15:25.350
I see.

00:15:25.350 --> 00:15:26.780
Then it's completed!

00:15:27.650 --> 00:15:28.810
Well done!

00:15:28.810 --> 00:15:32.310
Tell the men I said, "Well done."

00:15:32.310 --> 00:15:33.690
I will.

00:15:40.960 --> 00:15:44.920
<i>I shan't allow any more 
of Kishuu's civilians to suffer.</i>

00:15:46.860 --> 00:15:48.920
Since our faces are known,

00:15:49.470 --> 00:15:51.930
we shall remain hidden until the 
operation begins tomorrow.

00:15:52.510 --> 00:15:55.930
But I have the others running missions for us.

00:15:57.220 --> 00:16:02.430
Hibachi-dono and Irori-dono are 
securing a way into the castle.

00:16:04.200 --> 00:16:06.650
Koikawa-dono and Ichinotani-dono

00:16:06.650 --> 00:16:09.010
have gone into town to gather information.

00:16:09.800 --> 00:16:11.810
Yamagata-dono and Bizen-dono

00:16:11.810 --> 00:16:15.020
are using their connections to secure more aid.

00:16:17.020 --> 00:16:19.510
We've finally met up with everyone...

00:16:19.510 --> 00:16:21.660
Is there nothing I can do to help?

00:16:22.240 --> 00:16:24.080
Being hasty is very wrong.

00:16:24.470 --> 00:16:28.660
The real fight begins tomorrow, 
once the operation begins.

00:16:29.590 --> 00:16:30.670
Yes, sir!

00:16:31.070 --> 00:16:33.480
As for that operation,

00:16:33.480 --> 00:16:35.800
we'll be splitting into three groups.

00:16:35.800 --> 00:16:37.440
The Snow Group:

00:16:37.440 --> 00:16:43.310
the Magistrate's... servant...
 will go with Yamagata and Mugai-dono.

00:16:43.890 --> 00:16:45.390
Next, the Moon Group:

00:16:45.390 --> 00:16:49.820
This will be Bizen-dono, Irori-dono, 
and the Iwamatsu villagers.

00:16:50.440 --> 00:16:52.390
And finally, the Flower Group:

00:16:52.390 --> 00:16:55.820
All the City Patrol members 
except Mugai-dono.

00:16:56.440 --> 00:16:59.150
Tsukishima-dono, this is the 
fifth time I've gone over it.

00:16:59.150 --> 00:17:00.860
Do you finally understand?

00:17:00.860 --> 00:17:03.330
Yes! I'm in the Mountain Group, right?

00:17:08.760 --> 00:17:09.990
I got it wrong.

00:17:09.990 --> 00:17:12.180
I'm in the Flower Group.

00:17:12.180 --> 00:17:14.290
And this is where it gets important.

00:17:14.770 --> 00:17:16.820
I'll explain the roles of each team.

00:17:16.820 --> 00:17:18.140
Try to remember.

00:17:18.680 --> 00:17:20.320
Please do!

00:17:34.210 --> 00:17:38.530
How magnificent... How stately!

00:17:41.940 --> 00:17:43.900
Well, Sanada-dono?

00:17:43.900 --> 00:17:46.240
It is just what you wanted.

00:17:46.240 --> 00:17:49.970
No, we've made something even better.

00:17:51.460 --> 00:17:54.370
You have done well, Munenao-dono.

00:17:54.370 --> 00:17:57.600
I shall name it the <i>Black Butterfly</i>.

00:17:59.040 --> 00:18:02.400
We will hold a banquet, Munenao-dono.

00:18:02.400 --> 00:18:03.640
Prepare it.

00:18:05.440 --> 00:18:07.600
Wait, Sanada-dono.

00:18:07.600 --> 00:18:10.810
You said you would leave 
once the ship was ready!

00:18:11.240 --> 00:18:14.100
Will you break your promise again?

00:18:14.100 --> 00:18:15.870
This is the second time!

00:18:16.870 --> 00:18:19.570
You are the one who broke your promise.

00:18:20.340 --> 00:18:23.080
This is the deadline, the tenth day.

00:18:23.080 --> 00:18:26.080
<b>Wanted</b>

00:18:23.660 --> 00:18:26.080
And where are the fugitives?

00:18:27.520 --> 00:18:30.440
I will not break my promise.

00:18:30.440 --> 00:18:34.530
As promised, I will leave as 
soon as I have killed

00:18:34.530 --> 00:18:36.590
all the people in Kishuu.

00:18:39.370 --> 00:18:44.120
Now, gather all the townspeople.

00:18:44.120 --> 00:18:47.230
We will have a splendid banquet.

00:18:47.230 --> 00:18:49.100
Ah, my lord...

00:18:49.100 --> 00:18:50.230
What is it, Juuzou?

00:18:50.520 --> 00:18:54.860
Since we're having a banquet, 
may I go eat some snacks?

00:18:56.710 --> 00:19:01.690
Those men worked their hardest for me.

00:19:02.720 --> 00:19:06.020
At least be sure to chew thoroughly.

00:19:07.220 --> 00:19:08.250
As you wish.

00:19:09.090 --> 00:19:11.670
Then let us go, Munenao-dono.

00:19:13.330 --> 00:19:15.750
<i>It's hopeless...</i>

00:19:15.750 --> 00:19:19.500
<i>Force is all that's left.</i>

00:19:19.500 --> 00:19:22.960
<i>Kishuu Province will gather 
its forces for a final battle!</i>

00:19:37.660 --> 00:19:42.030
<i>A-All hope is lost!</i>

00:20:00.110 --> 00:20:01.270
Listen!

00:20:01.270 --> 00:20:04.270
I will now punish all the people of Kishuu

00:20:04.270 --> 00:20:06.810
for their failure to capture the fugitives.

00:20:07.210 --> 00:20:09.810
You will be our meals.

00:20:11.740 --> 00:20:16.820
Every last organ and drop of blood 
in your bodies will feed us!

00:20:22.150 --> 00:20:25.450
Now feed, insects!

00:20:30.770 --> 00:20:33.330
Someone, save us!

00:20:33.670 --> 00:20:34.710
Right here!

00:20:38.170 --> 00:20:39.890
Matsukichi! Tamekichi!

00:20:39.890 --> 00:20:42.570
<i>Full-Power Slap!</i>

00:20:48.250 --> 00:20:50.470
You take the weak ones!

